{
  "rationale": "Model sensing and motion as separate plants, then use compact specifications to bind sensed obstacle conditions to exactly one safe action per recovery/exploration mode. The policy favors forward progress in clear space, uses occasional random_walk for coverage variation, routes every obstacle event through a recovery state, uses brief backward escape only for front blockage, and reserves full_rotate for a dedicated repeated-failure last-resort path.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate uncontrollable perception from controllable motion capability",
    "Use one-shot action states so open-loop pulses complete without being preempted by path_clear",
    "Bias clear-space behavior toward move_forward with occasional random_walk",
    "Handle obstacle_left with rotate_clockwise and obstacle_right with rotate_counterclockwise consistently",
    "Handle obstacle_front via dedicated recovery: first short backward escape, then directed turn, then retry progress",
    "Reserve full_rotate only in a dedicated stuck/last_resort specification after repeated front blockage"
  ],
